// Default refresh rate RRO (XDA #231, wake-up jitter).
//
// device/nubia/NX809J/overlay/frameworks/base/.../config.xml sets
// config_defaultRefreshRate / config_defaultPeakRefreshRate = 144, but that
// overlay is a PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS bake into framework-res.apk — the
// lowest layer of all. The stock vendor image we ship (donor vendor_a.img)
// carries a static RRO, /vendor/overlay/FrameworksResTarget_Vendor.apk
// (android.overlay.target), that redefines both to 120 / 240 and wins:
//
//   cmd overlay lookup android android:integer/config_defaultRefreshRate → 120
//   cmd overlay lookup android android:integer/config_defaultPeakRefreshRate → 240
//
// So DisplayModeDirector has been running a 120..240 policy all along, and
// SurfaceFlinger's content detection flips the panel 60↔120↔144 every few
// frames right after a wake (each mode switch costs frames → visible stutter
// of the unlock animation). Static RROs are applied in partition order
// system < vendor < odm < oem < product < system_ext, so this system_ext
// overlay outranks the vendor one and finally lands the 144 Hz defaults.
runtime_resource_overlay {
    name: "NX809JRefreshRateOverlay",
    resource_dirs: ["res"],
    system_ext_specific: true,
    sdk_version: "current",
}
